From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: norm_desc: honour the payload checksum error bit

ndesc_get_rx_status() ignores RDES0 bit 0 (H616 UM 6.3.6.1
RX_PAYLOAD_ERR: payload checksum or length wrong), so such a frame can
go up as CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY. Return csum_none and let the stack check
it.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
index de30dfd..562177f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/norm_desc.c
@@ -104,6 +104,9 @@ static int ndesc_get_rx_status(struct stmmac_extra_stats *x,
 	if (rdes0 & RDES0_VLAN_TAG)
 		x->vlan_tag++;
 #endif
+	/* Payload checksum (or length) error: let the stack verify it */
+	if (ret == good_frame && (rdes0 & RDES0_PAYLOAD_CSUM_ERR))
+		ret = csum_none;
 	return ret;
 }
 
